  "question": {
    "text": "If the circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>&#8477;</mi></math>&nbsp;passes through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and its centre lies on the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>, then the length of intercept made by the circle on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>11</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>",
